jobs.description:
Would you like to grow within a dynamic international environment where you play a key role in coordinating business activities?


Our client is looking for an Administrative Commercial Assistant who will be responsible for the administrative, logistical, and financial follow-up of commercial operations while acting as a true business partner to the trading team.


Your Responsibilities


Working closely with traders and various internal departments, you will manage and coordinate files from A to Z:


Coordinate administrative processes and ensure accurate contract follow-up;


Organize transportation and oversee logistical operations related to shipments;


Manage the financial follow-up of files, including invoicing, payment processing, hedge monitoring, and period closings;


Maintain daily contact with international clients, suppliers, and business partners;


Support traders by ensuring smooth and efficient handling of commercial dossiers;


Contribute to the continuous improvement of internal processes and collaboration between departments.




You have successful experience in an administrative, commercial, logistics, or customer support role;


You are well-organized, detail-oriented, and able to manage multiple priorities simultaneously;


You enjoy working as part of a team while maintaining a high level of autonomy;


You are solution-oriented and thrive in an international business environment;


You are fluent in English; any additional language is considered a strong asset;


You have an excellent command of Microsoft Office applications, particularly Excel.







Strong service-oriented mindset;


Proactive attitude and sense of initiative;


Ability to anticipate needs and solve problems efficiently;


Resilience and flexibility in managing unexpected situations;


Long-term commitment and willingness to contribute to the company's success.

• Conduct in-depth analyses of P&L, ROCE, and risk management for specific market segments, identifying trends and growth potential;
• Translate financial data into clear reports and presentations, providing strategic insights and recommendations;
• Optimize working capital and monitor key risks related to accumulated positions and essential raw materials;
• Manage the planning process, including periodic forecasts, annual budgeting, and strategic planning up to EBIT level;
• Contribute to key investment projects, including CAPEX and M&A, by providing financial expertise;
• Collaborate with the Reporting Factory to enhance reporting and analysis tools, ensuring consistency and accuracy;
• Act as a strong business partner by supporting market segments and facilitating strategic decisions with financial insights.

Must-haves:

• You hold a master’s degree in finance, business administration, or a related field;
• Acquire at least 4 years of experience in finance, preferably as a controller or business partner;
• Demonstrate strong analytical skills to translate financial data into strategic insights;
• Communicate fluently in Dutch, both written and spoken;
• Possess excellent communication skills to present complex financial concepts clearly;
• Collaborate effectively with cross-functional teams and senior management.
Nice-to-haves:

• Have experience working with SAP or similar ERP systems.
• Speak English or French in addition to Dutch.
• Show a proactive mindset with a hands-on approach to problem-solving.
• Bring experience in investment analysis, CAPEX, or M&A.
• he Demonstrate tability to optimize working capital and risk management.

Our client is a leading international FMCG organisation with a strong presence across Belgium and the Netherlands. The company operates in a dynamic, commercially driven environment and is part of a larger international group, offering exposure to both local and global finance processes.

Jobomschrijving

As a Freelance Commercial Business Controller, your responsibilities are:

• Lead the budgeting, forecasting and financial planning cycle for assigned functions ;
• Monitor actuals versus budget and forecast, identifying risks, deviations and opportunities ;
• Prepare and explain management reporting and financial performance insights ;
• Ensure accurate and timely month-end closing, including invoices and accruals ;
• Act as a proactive finance business partner to senior non-finance stakeholders ;
• Challenge and advise management on cost efficiency, investments and profitability ;
• Support strategic planning and translate business priorities into financial plans ;
• Contribute to finance transformation, process improvement and automation projects ;

A successful Freelance Commercial Business Controller should have:

• Bachelor's or Master's degree in Finance, Economics or a related field ;
• Minimum 5 years of relevant experience in controlling, business finance or a similar role ;
• Strong analytical and numerical skills with excellent attention to detail ;
• Solid understanding of business processes, controlling, reporting and accounting ;
• Strong ability to translate financial analysis into concrete business recommendations ;
• Comfortable presenting and challenging financial performance with senior stakeholders ;
• Fluent in Dutch and English; French is a plus ;
• Willing to travel occasionally between Belgium and the Netherlands

Our client is a leading European group specialised in professional training, skills development and business transformation, offering both standard and tailor-made learning solutions. The organisation works with a broad range of corporate and institutional clients across areas including management, HR, finance, legal, banking, marketing and digital transformation.

Jobomschrijving

As a Freelance Tender/Bid Manager your responsibilities are:

• Identify and assess relevant European and institutional tender opportunities ;
• Analyse tender documentation, requirements, evaluation criteria and submission procedures ;
• Lead the end-to-end tender process, from opportunity identification through submission ;
• Coordinate internal stakeholders and external experts involved in bid preparation ;
• Structure and coordinate high-quality technical and commercial proposals ;
• Ensure compliance with all administrative, procedural and technical tender requirements ;
• Develop clear bid strategies and coordinate the production of supporting documentation ;
• Manage timelines, deadlines and deliverables to ensure accurate and on-time submissions ;

A successful Freelance Tender/Bid Manager should have:

• Proven experience in Tender Management, Bid Management or European Bid Management ;
• Strong understanding of European public procurement and tender procedures ;
• Experience managing complex or high-value European/institutional tenders ;
• Excellent ability to analyse complex tender documentation and identify key requirements ;
• Experience in writing, structuring and coordinating complex proposals ;
• Strong organisational skills with excellent attention to detail and deadline management ;
• Ability to work independently and take ownership of the complete bid process ;
• Excellent English; additional European languages are an advantage ;
